{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Traveling Wave Equation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Traveling Wave Equation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"traveling wave equation traveling wave equation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Traveling Wave Equation.md","fileName":"Traveling Wave Equation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Traveling Wave Equation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-17 00:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Wave Motion and Geometric Optics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Wave Motion and Geometric Optics","foundationsofphysics.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Traveling Wave Equation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Traveling Wave Equation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"traveling wave equation traveling wave equation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Traveling Wave Equation.md","fileName":"Traveling Wave Equation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Traveling Wave Equation","heading":"Traveling Wave Equation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A sinusoidal wave traveling in the positive $x$ direction can be written\n\n$$y(x,t)=A\\cos(\\omega t-kx+\\phi_0).$$\n\nHere $A$ is amplitude, $\\omega=2\\pi f$, and $k=2\\pi/\\lambda$. A surface of constant phase moves at $v=\\omega/k=f\\lambda$. Reversing the sign before $kx$ reverses the propagation direction under this convention.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Wave Motion and Geometric Optics","foundationsofphysics.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Traveling Wave Equation.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Traveling Wave Equation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"traveling wave equation traveling wave equation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Traveling Wave Equation.md","fileName":"Traveling Wave Equation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Traveling Wave Equation","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[foundationsofphysics.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Wave Motion and Geometric Optics","foundationsofphysics.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}